Approved by the owner, 2026-09-29.

Proposals, in .claude/goals/2026-09-holdfast-research/, each approved as its Recommendation says, with these amendments:

- P1 proposal-triage.md: approved as proposed. 20 keep, S0179 merged into goal 10, 0 drop. PR #94 is cherry-picked first in goal 2, and goal 2 keeps all nine of its items. On the items it flagged:
  - S0178: preserve_mtime stays on by default. Build only the statement half: validate and startup state the effective choice. The default does not flip.
  - S0164: the new queue_order value is named savings_per_hour.
  - S0151: use Dependabot. A committed .github/dependabot.yml covers GitHub Actions, the Docker base images and Go modules, and opens PRs that are never merged. The ffmpeg pin stays with pin-health.yml. There is no app to install.
  - S0176: goal 2 builds the holdfast half and opens a PR in NSchatz/homelab for the TZ half, never merged. Merging it is a NEEDS-OWNER item.
- P2 proposal-hw-gates.md: approved, option (a): the same gates and floors for every encoder, per-encoder quality keys and an additive output fidelity gate, built in goal 4. Chosen deliberately, knowing T10 did not choose "same gates, no exceptions" as final.
- P3 proposal-amd-image.md: approved, option (a): the VAAPI/QSV runtime goes in the default amd64 image, with no -hw tag. AMD encodes through Mesa radeonsi with encoder: vaapi. amf stays for host installs and is refused in the image with a named reason. Chosen deliberately, knowing T45 did not choose VAAPI-only as final.
- P4 proposal-node-protocol.md: approved, option (a): HTTP+JSON leases on the existing server, with a holdfast worker subcommand.
- P5 proposal-crop-dv.md: approved, option (c): a Dolby Vision source is cropped only to the active area its own RPU names, with L5 zeroed and gated. Every other DV source keeps the I7 refusal and encodes uncropped.
- P6 proposal-docs-corpus.md: approved, option (a): internal/corpus skips .claude/, carried by goal 2.

Inferred rows I1-I20: accepted as written. I6 is confirmed: DV profile 8 and HDR10+ are carried by default on the cpu encoder once the metadata gates pass.
